{"title":"Chi-squared distribution","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Chi-Square test</b> is a statistical test used to compare the observed numerical data and the expected numerical data to look for a relationship between categorical variables and determine statistically significant differences.\n</p><p>The chi-square value is given as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a61c1e51680e27d35d05bebed87d474972fc70bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\chi^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"20\" />. The formula to calculate the chi-square value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82dc63f34514d9af56cfece59e250de61b8feda3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\chi^2=\\sum\\dfrac{(o-e)^2}{e}\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chi-squared_distribution&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distribution&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Distribution (page does not exist)\">Distribution</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Chi-squared_distribution&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018080330\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 19/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion